  "description": "Rejected inputs (spec §10). expected_error is the VerifyError or SizeError variant name. A size failure is the SizeError name. source_data_size rebuilds the tree. data_size, chunk_index, segment_index, commitment, and proof are the verifier inputs. The mutation names how those differ from the honest proof. The 64-byte segment is left concatenated with right, checked against the commitment of node(left, right). That segment is a leaf (spec §3). The unanchored case records the re-derived commitment, which verifies, and the anchored commitment, which does not (spec §6). A pinned in-chunk sibling that is not empty(ℓ) is checked against the commitment of that proof. The stand-in hash is 32 bytes of 0xAB. One case is level 0 and one is a higher level (spec §5). Test geometry, n = 20, leaf 3 is that hash: segments 2 and 3 fail. Segments 0 and 1 of that upload verify; they are in the segment-proof file. An honest chunk proof and an honest segment proof whose last hash is size_witness(G, n+1) fail before the climb. data_size = max_data_size + 1 is out of range. That case records a one-chunk maximum. chunk_proof_at_moved_index: the bytes and proof of chunk 2 of n = 96, the last hash size_witness(G, 64), shown as chunk 1 of n' = 64 against the commitment re-derived for 64. The steps match, and the chunk leaf hashes the index, so it fails (spec §6). size_proof_wrong_size_<check>_<n>_as_<n'>: for n in 1, 8, 9, 32, 33, 112, and 157, the honest rightmost chunk or rightmost data segment of the n'-byte upload and its proof, at the indexes computed from n', against node(data_tree_root(n), size_witness(G, n')). n' is n - 1, n + 1, the nearest size with another chunk count, and the nearest segment boundary with the same chunk count (spec §9 size proof). chunk_root_as_leaf: honest one-chunk bytes and proof against node(chunk_root(bytes), size_witness(G, n)); the one-chunk root is chunk_leaf(0, R_0). rightmost_segment_padding_slot: the honest siblings of segment 3 of n 